            "body": "This PR has been automatically converted to **draft** because all PRs must start as drafts.\n\nWhen you are ready for review, click **Ready for Review** to begin the review process. This will:\n1. Add the oncall reviewer (optional reviewer)\n2. Add required review teams based on your changes\n\nSee the [contribution guide](https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/blob/main/docs/developer/submit.md) for more details.",
            "createdAt": "2026-03-16T21:18:11Z",
            "databaseId": 4070650490,
            "updatedAt": "2026-03-16T21:18:11Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/3892#issuecomment-4070650490"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "cluster2600"
            },
            "body": "### Tested on NVIDIA GB10 (DGX Spark), PyTorch 2.10, Python 3.12\n\n**Before fix** — bug reproduced with a minimal script that inits dist, creates a `PersistentAsyncCaller`, destroys the process group, then calls `close()`:\n\n```\nException ignored in: <function PersistentAsyncCaller.__del__ at 0xe15f200a6480>\n  File \".../async_utils.py\", line 497, in close\n    f\"PersistentAsyncCaller: {torch.distributed.get_rank()}, Destroying Async Caller\"\nValueError: Default process group has not been initialized\n```\n\nBoth explicit `close()` and `__del__` via GC crash.\n\n**After fix** — clean exit, no errors:\n\n```\nprocess group destroyed\ncalling close() after dist teardown...\nSUCCESS: close() completed without error\nletting __del__ fire via del...\ndone\n```",
            "createdAt": "2026-03-16T21:24:40Z",
            "databaseId": 4070680604,
            "updatedAt": "2026-03-16T21:24:40Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/3892#issuecomment-4070680604"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "cluster2600"
            },
            "body": "Closing in favour of #3781, which takes a broader approach — it introduces a centralised `_get_rank_or_unknown()` helper and covers `AsyncCaller`, `TemporalAsyncCaller`, and `PersistentAsyncCaller` rather than just the last one.\n\nThe DGX Spark test results posted here are still valid and I've added them to #3781 as well. Cheers!",
            "createdAt": "2026-03-16T22:04:48Z",
            "databaseId": 4070919319,
            "updatedAt": "2026-03-16T22:04:48Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/Megatron-LM/pull/3892#issuecomment-4070919319"
          }
